# Default: normalise text files to LF in the repository, let Git convert on
# checkout per the platform. This does NOT apply to .star, overridden below.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Stardata files carry their own line-ending policy (spec §2: LF or CRLF are
# both legal, and an implementation MUST NOT normalise them on round-trip).
# `-text` tells Git to leave these bytes alone entirely — no line-ending
# conversion on checkout or checkin, regardless of core.autocrlf, regardless
# of platform. See A4 / CONTRIBUTING.md#line-endings.
*.star -text

# Binary-ish or generated formats: no diff noise, no text conversion.
*.png binary
*.spak binary
